{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q423029","formula":"C₂H₂F₄","hill":"C2H2F4","elements":["H","C","F"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"F":4.0,"H":2.0},"names":{"en":"Norflurane","ru":"Тетрафторэтан"},"descriptions":{"en":"1,1,1,2-Tetrafluoroethane (also known as norflurane (INN), R-134a, Klea 134a, Freon 134a, Forane 134a, Genetron 134a, Green Gas, Florasol 134a, Suva 134a, HFA-134a, or HFC-134a) is a hydrofluorocarbon (HFC) and haloalkane refrigerant with thermodynamic properties similar to R-12 (dichlorodifluoromethane) but with insignificant ozone depletion potential and a lower 100-year global warming potential (1,430, compared to R-12's GWP of 10,900). It has the formula CF3CH2F and a boiling point of −26.3 °C (−15.34 °F) at atmospheric pressure. R-134a cylinders are colored light blue.","ru":"1,1,1,2-Тетрафторэта́н (также известный как несимметричный тетрафторэтан и под обозначениями R-134a, HFC-134a) — гидрофтороуглерод, фторированный алкан с формулой CF3—CFH2. Относится к фторорганическим соединениям и является фторуглеводородом этанового ряда. Служит альтернативной заменой озоноразрушающим хлорфторуглеродам."},"fame":32,"pubchemCid":13129,"mass":102.03,"charge":0,"smiles":"C(C(F)(F)F)F","inchikey":"LVGUZGTVOIAKKC-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1,1,1,2-tetrafluoroethane","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"13129","atoms":8,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.452,"y":-0.855,"z":-0.047,"el":"F"},{"x":-0.501,"y":0.721,"z":1.124,"el":"F"},{"x":-0.48,"y":0.822,"z":-1.056,"el":"F"},{"x":1.929,"y":0.108,"z":0.003,"el":"F"},{"x":-0.396,"y":-0.017,"z":-0.002,"el":"C"},{"x":0.899,"y":-0.778,"z":-0.022,"el":"C"},{"x":0.991,"y":-1.38,"z":-0.93,"el":"H"},{"x":0.99,"y":-1.431,"z":0.85,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,4,1],[1,4,1],[2,4,1],[3,5,1],[4,5,1],[5,6,1],[5,7,1]]},"sources":[{"role":